@startuml 10_state_connection
title State Model: Connection Lifecycle (FR-12, UC-1, UC-5)
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description
skinparam state<<planned>> {
  BackgroundColor #EEEEEE
  BorderColor #888888
  FontColor #666666
}

[*] --> TcpOpen : accepted (IP limit and semaphore passed)
TcpOpen --> Connected : ConnectRequest\n[major version matches]\n/ ConnectResponse
TcpOpen --> Closed : ConnectRequest [major differs]\n/ ErrorResponse(INVALID_PROTOCOL_VERSION)
TcpOpen --> Closed : no frame within FirstMessageTimeout (5 s)
Connected --> Connected : AuthRequest [empty display_name]\n/ ErrorResponse(INVALID_ARGUMENT)
Connected --> Authenticated : AuthRequest [valid]\n/ AuthResponse

state Authenticated {
  [*] --> NoSession
  NoSession --> InSession : JoinSessionRequest [joinable]\n/ StateUpdate
  NoSession --> NoSession : JoinSessionRequest [unknown game, bad id, full]\n/ ErrorResponse
  InSession --> NoSession : LeaveSessionRequest\n/ LeaveSessionResponse
  state InSession {
    [*] --> InLobby
    InLobby --> InMatch : Game.ReadyToStart is true\n/ StateUpdate(IN_PROGRESS)
    InMatch --> InLobby : terminal outcome\n/ MatchResult
    InMatch --> InMatch : ActionRequest\n/ StateUpdate or ErrorResponse
  }
}

state "Disconnected\n(grace period)" as Disconnected <<planned>>
Authenticated --> Disconnected : socket lost [in a session]
Disconnected --> Authenticated : AuthRequest(player_id, token) matches
Disconnected --> Closed : grace period expires

TcpOpen --> Closed : read error, EOF
Connected --> Closed : read timeout, EOF
Authenticated --> Closed : read timeout (ReadTimeout), EOF,\nwrite error, or out queue full (slow client)
Closed --> [*]

note bottom of Connected
  In every state a message that is not valid there
  (for example JoinSessionRequest before AuthResponse,
  or a second ConnectRequest) gets ErrorResponse(INVALID_STATE)
  and the state does not change.
end note
@enduml
